#: inc/skin.php:132
msgid "Quillwork is a quiet, literary theme for people whose work is words — writers, editors, and anyone building a personal brand around what they have to say. I built it to get out of the way: a calm reading column, type that breathes, and nothing on the page fighting your sentences. It's given freely, in the hope it earns you a few more readers. Here's how to make it yours."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: linked "Settings → Reading" admin screen.
#: inc/skin.php:143
#, php-format
msgid "A visitor's first second decides whether they stay. If you have a piece you're proud of, or a short introduction to who you are, send them there first. Set a static front page under %s, and point your posts page somewhere of its own."
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:144
msgid "Settings → Reading"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: linked "Site Editor" admin screen.
#: inc/skin.php:151
#, php-format
msgid "A site without a menu is a room without doors. Open the %s, edit the header, and assign your menu to Primary Navigation so readers can find the rest of your work."
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:152
#: inc/skin.php:189
msgid "Site Editor"
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:156
msgid "Start from a good page, not a blank one."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: linked "new page" admin screen.
#: inc/skin.php:159
#, php-format
msgid "A blank page is the hardest place to begin. Quillwork ships with patterns — pre-built sections you can drop in and edit. %s, click the block inserter, open Patterns, and look for the Quillwork group. Start there and change the words."
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:160
msgid "Start a new page"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: linked "Site Editor → Styles" admin screen.
#: inc/skin.php:167
#, php-format
msgid "The default palette and fonts are a starting point, not a verdict. In the Site Editor, open %s to change colours and typefaces until the site feels like your voice and not mine. Nothing you do here can break the theme — it's a safe place to experiment."
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:168
msgid "Styles"
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:172
msgid "Add featured images so the card grids sing."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: linked "Posts" admin screen.
#: inc/skin.php:175
#, php-format
msgid "Quillwork lays your posts out as cards, and a card without an image is a card with a hole in it. Add a featured image to each of %s — even a simple, calm one — and the grids come to life."
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:176
msgid "your posts"
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:182
msgid "Here's the honest part: Quillwork is already fast, and that's by design, not by accident. It ships zero JavaScript, hosts its own fonts so nothing phones home to Google. You don't have to do anything to get that."
msgstr ""

#: inc/skin.php:183
msgid "To keep it that way: be gentle with plugins that add scripts to every page, size your images before you upload them, and resist the urge to bolt on a page builder — the theme is the layout. On accessibility, Quillwork gives you real focus outlines, a skip link, sensible heading order, and motion that respects a visitor's reduce-motion setting. Keep your own copy and images to that bar and the whole site stays welcoming to everyone."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: linked "Site Editor" admin screen.
#: inc/skin.php:188
#, php-format
msgid "Quillwork leaves a small credit in your footer. It's a thank-you, not a tax — it helps people find the theme, which is the only payment I ask. If it doesn't suit your site, remove it in two clicks: open the %s, edit the Footer, and delete the line. Developers can filter quillwork/footer_credit_text instead. No hard feelings either way."
msgstr ""

